Package: pathlab
Type: Package
Title: Point-and-Click PLS-SEM, CB-SEM, Statistics and More in the Browser
Version: 1.2.10
Authors@R: person("Harry Barton", "Essel", email = "bartoness.knust.fes.eist@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: PathLab SEM runs on your own computer and opens in your web browser, in the way
    'bibliometrix::biblioshiny()' does. You draw a path model on a canvas and estimate it with
    'seminr' (PLS-SEM), 'lavaan' (CB-SEM) or 'cSEM' (GSCA). The app also offers statistics with the
    'jmv' engine, qualitative comparative analysis, latent profile and class analysis, machine
    learning, bibliometrics, and text and qualitative data analysis. Your data never leave your
    computer: start the app with run().
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
SystemRequirements: A web browser. Optional: Quarto (Word reports), a 64-bit Java (WEKA learners).
